A||||4||lowfunds||Lowering Spindles||||1||
Z||000000||lowfunds||06-08-2001||04:17 PM||||I have a question for anyone running drop spindles in the front. It lowers the front 2in correct? but does your wheel well gap stay the same as stock? And if so what do you do to run 17's with say 215-45s run coilovers? Will this allow for clearance? Thanks for any help.......||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||06-08-2001||11:51 PM||||It is not physically possible to lower a car 2" without reducing wheel gap by the same amount. <P>As for 17"s, I don't know, but I hope they'll fit. Anyone know for sure?<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tweek||06-09-2001||02:54 AM||||Unless of course you lower the car by digging trenches in the grouns for the wheels to be in.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||06-09-2001||11:13 PM||||17's will work, 205-40's work on mine w/Street Dreams 2" drop spindles.  I think 215 45's would also fit, but would rub over the big bumps.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 06-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||gt2437||06-14-2001||08:32 AM||||I have had 215/45/zr17 on the front with no rubbing or clearance issues (38mm offset on 7" wide rim). I am now running 225/45/zr17 (all the way around) and it rubs slightly when the wheel is fully turned.<BR>I have 2" lowering springs from the Fiero Store. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1486717&a=11524521&p=47383359&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
